WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.397
A retry must change something.

00:00:02.397 --> 00:00:06.652
Attempt one should usually use the user's original wording.

00:00:06.652 --> 00:00:13.512
If that fails, attempt two may rewrite the query with clearer vocabulary or more specific terms.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:21.087
If that still fails, attempt three may change a filter, retrieval strategy, or approved source.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.791
Then stop safely.

00:00:23.319 --> 00:00:26.261
Think of retries as controlled experiments.

00:00:26.261 --> 00:00:32.001
Each attempt should test a different hypothesis about why the previous retrieval failed.

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:37.946
If the only change is calling the exact same function again with the exact same inputs,

00:00:37.946 --> 00:00:40.120
you are not learning anything new.

00:00:41.036 --> 00:00:48.698
A good trace should make those differences obvious: original query, rewritten query, alternate source,

00:00:48.698 --> 00:00:50.558
and final stop reason.
